  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "No matched oral versus intravenous AUC data are available for the query.",
    "First-pass metabolism and systemic clearance are not directly measured for the query.",
    "L4 records are fraction-absorbed/dissolution data, not systemic F measurements.",
    "No query-specific efflux or intestinal metabolism data are available."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "High: the query is a sulfanilamide/isoxazole analog of sulfonamide drugs with consistently high fraction absorbed in L4 records (85% to ~100%), and the closest prior F contexts (PABA, PAS) show high oral bioavailability; no affirmative evidence supports F < 20%, so the prediction remains high and is strengthened by the L4 absorption evidence."
